<table>
<tr><th>Case</th><th>What is on the board</th><th>Resolution</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>m1(int) vs m1(float)</td><td>Exact match first; else automatic promotion (char→int, long→float); double cannot widen further → CE cannot find symbol</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>m1(String) vs m1(Object)</td><td>Exact match; null → child (String) beats parent</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>m1(String) vs m1(StringBuffer)</td><td>Exact match; null → ambiguous (same-level siblings)</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>m1(int,float) vs m1(float,int)</td><td>Exact match; 10,10 both match → ambiguous; 10.5f,10.5f neither matches → cannot find symbol</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>m1(int) vs m1(int...)</td><td>Var-arg is least priority (like switch default); old 1.0 general method beats 1.5 var-arg</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>m1(Animal) vs m1(Monkey)</td><td>Compiler uses reference type; runtime object plays no role</td></tr>
</table>
